# Trivy vulnerability waivers. One ID per line, each with a reason and a
# removal condition. Trivy auto-discovers this file; ci.yml also points at it
# explicitly via the trivy-action `trivyignores` input.

# GHSA-wrw7-89jp-8q8g / RUSTSEC-2024-0429 — MEDIUM
# glib < 0.20.0: unsoundness in glib::VariantStrIter's Iterator impl. UB only
# under a specific misuse pattern this codebase does not exercise (we never
# touch glib::Variant directly).
# Transitive dependency: pulled in by Tauri's GTK/webview stack (frontend/
# src-tauri/Cargo.lock), not a direct choice. A manual bump in Cargo.lock is
# reverted on the next `cargo update` — the real fix waits on Tauri bumping its
# own glib dependency.
# Tracked continuously as Dependabot alert #1. Delete this line once Tauri
# ships with glib 0.20+ and `cargo update` clears it.
GHSA-wrw7-89jp-8q8g

# GHSA-q8mj-m7cp-5q26 / GHSA-x5fp-wj9c-mxmx / GHSA-4mjr-xmp4-gh2g — MODERATE
# qs 2.2.5-6.15.3: remotely-triggerable DoS in qs.stringify/array-limit parsing.
# Transitive dependency: pulled in by @stryker-mutator/core@10.0.0 (frontend's new mutation-
# testing dev dependency, 2026-09-14) via typed-rest-client@2.3.1, not a direct choice —
# `npm audit fix --dry-run` confirms no resolvable upgrade path exists yet (typed-rest-client
# hasn't bumped its own qs range). Not reachable in this project's context either way: Stryker
# only runs as a local/CI dev-tool against this repo's own source, never processes untrusted
# request data the way qs.stringify's advisory scenario requires. Delete these lines once
# @stryker-mutator/core bumps typed-rest-client (or typed-rest-client itself bumps qs) and
# `npm audit` clears it.
GHSA-q8mj-m7cp-5q26
GHSA-x5fp-wj9c-mxmx
